Project Concept

A Project represents a game or content unit (example: ChatDuell, QuizDuell, etc.).

Project fields:

name

description

status (planning / active / paused / released / archived)

owner_id (Robin)

created_by

Each project contains:

Ideas

Tasks / Follow-ups

Files

Comments

Idea & Follow-up Workflow (CRITICAL)

This is the heart of the system.

Idea flow:

Robin creates an idea

Example:

Game name: ChatDuell
Flow:
1. User joins
2. Question appears
3. Chat votes
4. Winner shown


Idea status starts as:

New

Main Dev reviews

Marks:

In Progress

Needs Info

Done

Partially Done

Follow-ups

Robin can reply with:

Bugs

Errors

New features

Main Dev follows up again

Same pattern for:

Designer

Video Editor

This must behave like a threaded timeline, NOT a simple comment section.

Unified Follow-up System (ALL ROLES USE SAME SYSTEM)

Robin posts initial request

Assigned person responds

Robin replies again if needed

Status updates at each step

Follow-up entry fields:

user_id

content (markdown supported)

status_at_time

attachments (optional)

created_at

